            </note>
            <note corresp="#d50-f2" n="2" xml:id="d50-f2-content">
                <p>November 21.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d50-f3" n="3" xml:id="d50-f3-content">
                <p>Reference is to the operetta composed by Bernstein based on Voltaire’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Candide</hi>. It opened on Broadway on December 1, 1956, at the Martin Beck
                    Theater. (Louis Calta, “Candide to Open at Beck Tonight,” <hi
                        rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>, December 1, 1956, p. 18)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
